      "message": "nit: to_hex_str seemed more descriptive.\n\nAlso looking at the `repr` implementation in Bumble this doesn\u0027t seems to be doing the same thing\n\nhttps://github.com/google/bumble/blob/ca063eda0b84640e69f066160aa3564474b0b628/bumble/core.py#L268\n\nAs ASHA is a 16 bit UUID, I expect this to be giving `UUID-16:FDF0`\n\nLooking at bit more it seems that if the UUID has a name it gives it\u0027s name instead.\n\n```\nGATT_ASHA_SERVICE \u003d UUID.from_16_bits(0xFDF0, \u0027Audio Streaming for Hearing Aid\u0027)\n```\n\nSo for me `repr(GATT_ASHA_SERVICE)` gives you `Audio Streaming for Hearing Aid` which seems even more wrong.\n\nWhat am I missing here ?",
